  "recipeCuisine": "Spain",
  "name": "Paella Valenciana",
  "text": "Paella Valenciana\n\nPreparation time: 30 mins to 1 hour\n\nCooking time: 10 to 30 mins\n\nYield: 6-8\n\nIngredients\n\n60 g chorizo (cut into thin slices) - optional,\n\n4 garlic cloves (peeled and lightly crushed and chopped),\n\n1 brown onion (finely diced),\n\n1 red pepper (diced or sliced),\n\n2 tomatoes,\n\n100g runner beans,\n\n1 tsp smoked paprika,\n\n200 g calasparra (Spanish short-grain) rice,\n\n75 ml oz dry white wine,\n\n750 ml chicken stock (heated with ¼ tsp saffron threads),\n\n6 boneless chicken thighs (halved and browned),\n\n30 g fresh or frozen peas\n\nolive oil,\n\n2 tbsp chopped flat-leaf parsley,\n\nSalt and freshly ground black pepper\n\nLemon wedges.\n\nPreparation method\n\n1. Heat half the olive oil in a paella dish or heavy-based saucepan.\n\n2. If using, cook the chorizo a little to flavour the oil.\n\n3. Add chicken thighs and brown.\n\n4. Add the pepper and beans.\n\n5. Add the onion and heat until softened.\n\n6. Add the garlic and smoked paprika and heat until aromatic.\n\n7. Add the passata and warm through.\n\n8. Add calasparra rice, and stir until all the grains of rice are nicely coated and glossy.\n\n9. Add the stock and simmer, adding more liquid if necessary, until the rice is cooked.\n\n10. When done, turn up the heat to medium and cook for a further minute.\n\n11. Remove from the heat, cover with foil and a cloth and rest for 7 minutes.\n\n12. Scatter the chopped parsley over the paella and serve.",
  "recipeYield": "6-8",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "60 g chorizo (cut into thin slices) - optional,",
